## Dependency arrows

```
cmd -> internal/control | cmd/*/main
ingest hot path must NOT import controlplane admin or internal/fraud scoring
pkg/* must NOT import internal/*

reportjob -> reports (one-way; reports does not import reportjob)
campaign -> reports, reportjob, flow, controlplane/authz (not controlplane root)
campaign -X-> controlplane (no import cycle)
flow -X-> controlplane (no import cycle)
fraudadmin -X-> controlplane (no import cycle)
billingadmin -> campaign (balance DTO aliases); -X-> controlplane
opsadmin -> campaign, fraudadmin; -X-> controlplane
reconciliation -> governance (quota repair tick); -X-> controlplane
governance -X-> controlplane (no import cycle)
smartalerts -X-> controlplane (no import cycle)
controlplane -> campaign, flow, reports, reportjob, fraudadmin, billingadmin, opsadmin, smartalerts, governance, reconciliation (composition root)
```

Tracker (`internal/ingestion`) must not import `internal/controlplane` admin handlers or `internal/fraud` scoring. `pkg/*` is shared utilities only - no `internal/*` imports.

## Future target (do not implement opportunistically)

Remaining split candidates (not done):

- `ingestion` -> `ingest/`, `filter/`, `stream/`, `track/`
- Move remaining `service_campaign.go` experiment cohort helpers onto `campaign` or keep in controlplane

Package cap when splitting: ~40 files or ~8k LOC per package; one domain per package.

**Mandatory:** `doc.go` at the root of every production package (`package <name>` only). Sync via `scripts/dev/sync_package_doc_go.py`.

Excluded: generated subtrees only (`db/`, `pb/`, `queries/` under a domain package — they do not get their own `doc.go`).

**Hard ban:** god packages and unbounded `controlplane` growth (`modular-monolith.mdc`). New admin code lands in the domain package first; bridges only wire.

**Hard ban:** micro-packages and premature splits — new `internal/<domain>/` only when minimum viable extraction ships in the same change set (`modular-monolith.mdc`).

